---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const description =
  'How CalcPulse handles affiliate links, and what a link on this site does and does not mean.';
---

<BaseLayout title="Affiliate disclosure — CalcPulse" description={description}>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 sm:px-6 py-12">
    <nav class="text-sm text-ink-400" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-ink-600">Home</a> <span aria-hidden="true">/</span> Disclosure
    </nav>
    <h1 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink-950">Affiliate disclosure</h1>

    <div class="prose prose-ink mt-6">
      <p>
        Some links on CalcPulse are affiliate links. If you follow one and buy something, the vendor may
        pay this site a commission at no extra cost to you. Where a page carries such links, the page
        says so near them.
      </p>

      <h2>What that changes, and what it does not</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          It does not change the price you pay, and it does not give this site access to your account or
          your data.
        </li>
        <li>
          It does not decide which tools are covered. A guide is written because a question is worth
          answering, not because a programme pays for it.
        </li>
        <li>
          It does not soften a verdict. If a tool is the wrong choice for a scenario, the page says so
          on the same page that carries the link.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Calculators are not products</h2>
      <p>
        Nothing on this site is sold directly. There is no checkout here, there are no advertising
        slots, and the site never asks for card details. Paid guides and template packs are sold
        through Gumroad, which appears on its own domain with its own checkout. If you ever see payment
        fields presented as CalcPulse, close the page — they are not ours.
      </p>

      <h2>No advertising network</h2>
      <p>
        The site carries no ad network tags, so no advertiser sees which page you read and no third-party
        script runs on these pages. Any commercial relationship behind a link is stated next to the link
        itself.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
